+/* Slice dividers: five drawn gold lines of one width (an SVG), not a conic-gradient hairline. A 0.5deg gradient sliver
+   is thinner than a pixel at the hub and fat at the rim, and when the track turns the GPU resamples it into a dashed,
+   flickering line (this is what the eye reads as a rough spin). Real strokes with round caps stay one clean line at
+   every angle; the track also keeps its own layer for the whole transition so nothing is re-rasterised mid-spin. */
 #leagueWheelScreen.v26Skin .wheelTrack {
   z-index: 1;
   display: block;
